      "reason": "THIS BATCH REPORTED A PASSED PREDICTION AND THEN FALSIFIED IT ITSELF, AND THE FIRST REPORT REACHED A COMMIT MESSAGE, A SESSION RECORD AND A PR BODY BEFORE THE CHECK THAT BROKE IT. REF-00979's 19-of-30 was counted with a screen whose regex carries 'propuls' and 'accessib', so it was measuring 'cites wheelchair-propulsion papers' -- trivially true of a wheelchair-propulsion paper. Under a strict slope-only screen it is 2 of 30. The two later pre-registered predictions both failed in opposite directions, which is what prompted testing the instrument rather than the hypothesis. The correction is GAP-029 and the session record; commit 857050c states the false version and cannot be edited. WHAT SHOULD HAVE HAPPENED: the screen should have been validated before any yield figure was reported as evidence for anything, because a screen is an instrument and an untested instrument produces numbers, not measurements."
    },
    {
      "rule": "integrity-protocol",
      "reason": "THE FIRST HALF OF THIS BATCH WAS SHORT OF MINIMUM VIABLE AND I CLOSED IT ANYWAY. DR-2026-08-19 section 12.2 sets minimum viable at 10-12 searches and 3-4 admissions; the first half ran 4 and admitted 0, wrote a session record, an attestation and a PR, and reported it as complete. One failed retrieval was allowed to bound the batch while GAP-025 had eight deferrals outstanding and the register held three candidates that resolved through Crossref on the first try in the second half. The user identified it; I did not. The continuation reaches 8 searches and 2 admissions, still under minimum viable on searches."
    },
